[Music]  perpetual  still can't believe they're all here and  all well  in march she was rushed to hospital with  covid  she ended up on a ventilator in an  induced coma  and her babies were born by cesarean  section  she thought they hadn't made it  i was pregnant at 24 5 weeks at that  stage  by the time i woke up i was so  disoriented because  i couldn't i lost my pregnancy  so i couldn't see my bump anymore i was  really really worried and disoriented  the babies pascal and palmer were so  premature they were placed in incubators  on the special care unit  their mum spent another 16 days on  critical care  before eventually meeting them  they were so tiny  they didn't look anywhere like my  previous two other kids  so i couldn't touch them i couldn't  the nurse had to get my hand to touch  them  and i felt so emotional what was your  reaction  when you found out um that perpetual had  pulled through but  but also that the twins had survived as  well  so i'm happy the dreams were there  they've been delivered  but the thing is is my wife coming home  at that point it was not clear to me go  but she did come home they all did  much to their older brother and sister's  delight  sometime when i look at them i  get them in tears because  i never knew they would make it  and you know it's amazing  perpetual herself a hospital consultant  says she and the twins are now well  and their laughter is just the tonic  after the months of worry  they've all been through  lisa dowd sky news birmingham

